⚠️  REPLACE THIS FILE WITH THE FULL GPL v3 TEXT BEFORE PUBLISHING.

The full canonical text lives at  https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt
(roughly 700 lines, ~35 KB).

The easiest way to get it correct is to use GitHub's UI when you create
the repo:

    1. Create the repo on github.com.
    2. In the "Add a license" step, pick "GNU General Public License v3.0".
    3. GitHub commits the full canonical text as LICENSE for you.

Alternatively, from PowerShell after cloning the empty repo:

    Invoke-WebRequest -Uri https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt -OutFile LICENSE
    git add LICENSE && git commit -m "Add full GPL-3.0 license text"
